/**
 * Numeric value 0..9 of a Unicode decimal digit, or -1 if the code point is
 * not a decimal digit at all.
 *
 * ASCII takes the fast path. For everything else we exploit the fact that the
 * `Nd` category is laid out as contiguous, 10-aligned runs: we walk back to the
 * start of the enclosing run and take the offset modulo 10. The modulo matters
 * for U+1D7CE..U+1D7FF, where five mathematical digit sets (bold,
 * double-struck, sans-serif, sans-serif bold, monospace) sit back to back in
 * one 50-code-point block.
 *
